<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gelou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gelou is a ruler described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a>, written around 1200, as a Vlach duke in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> at the time of the Hungarian conquest around 900. According to the chronicle he was defeated by the Hungarian chieftain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuhutum">Tuhutum</a> and killed while fleeing, after which his people accepted Tuhutum as their lord. No other source mentions him, and historians dispute whether he existed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gelou.jpg" alt="Gelou" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Țetcu Mircea Rareș · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GilauCJ2013_(4).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
